\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {5.8}RQ\ref {rq:demography}: does demographic pressure suffice}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces The transition under a closed population, under vital rates applied to single-body households, and under the full household demography of \S  \ref {sec:demography}; and, in the right-hand panel, under endogenous births with the class mechanism damped as in RQ\ref {rq:alliance}. A transition proceeding with population fixed is Brenner's anti-demographic claim; one requiring endogenous births is Postan's.}}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rq7}{{11}{30}{}{figure.11}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {5.9}RQ\ref {rq:symbiosis}: the edges of symbiosis}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Landlord and tenant accumulation across the sweep of the extraction share $\theta _{\text  {rent}}$. A band in which both rise is Brenner's English symbiosis; its upper edge, beyond which extraction destroys the tenant's capacity to improve and with it the lord's rent roll, is the boundary Brenner asserts without locating.}}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rq8}{{12}{30}{}{figure.12}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {5.10}RQ\ref {rq:enclosure}: enclosure as driver or consequence}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces The landless share and its composition with enclosure suppressed ($\nu _1=\nu _2=\nu _3=0$) against the baseline, and the timing of $\Xi (t)$ against the timing of rent-conversion-driven dispossession. A landless pool of comparable size without enclosure supports Shaw-Taylor against Wood on the separability of the two channels.}}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rq10}{{13}{30}{}{figure.13}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {5.11}Claims about the model}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces The diagnostics of \S  \ref {sec:rq-model}: aggregate tenure composition, the attribution of the farm-size Gini to engrossment rather than turnover, the wage and rent series against each other, and the population accounting -- the share of parcels no household can take up, and the cross-seed correlation between tenure outcomes and population. A failure in any panel is a defect to repair before the results above can be read.}}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:checks}{{14}{30}{}{figure.14}{}}
